========================================
ASSIGNMENT 4
Deploy a Simple Smart Contract to the Ethereum Blockchain
========================================

1. Open Remix IDE:
https://remix.ethereum.org

2. Create Solidity file:
SimpleStorage.sol

3. Write the following code:

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract SimpleStorage {

    uint public data;

    function setData(uint _data) public {
        data = _data;
    }

    function getData() public view returns(uint) {
        return data;
    }
}

4. Open Solidity Compiler tab.

5. Compile SimpleStorage.sol.

6. Open Deploy & Run Transactions tab.

7. Select Environment:
Remix VM

8. Select Contract:
SimpleStorage

9. Click Deploy.

10. Expand deployed contract.

11. Enter a number in setData() function.

12. Click setData button.

13. Click getData() function.

14. Verify returned value successfully.
```
